msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:12
msgid ""
"Full functionality has been added to the driver. Since some of the Controls "
"and startup options are ALSA-Standard, only the special Controls are "
"described and discussed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:18
msgid "Hardware functionality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:21
msgid "Audio transmission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:23
msgid "number of channels -- depends on transmission mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:25
msgid ""
"The number of channels chosen is from 1..Nmax. The reason to use for a lower "
"number of channels is only resource allocation, since unused DMA channels "
"are disabled and less memory is allocated. So also the throughput of the PCI "
"system can be scaled. (Only important for low performance boards)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:31
msgid "Single Speed -- 1..64 channels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:34
msgid ""
"Choosing the 56-channel mode for transmission or as receiver, only 56 are "
"transmitted/received over the MADI, but all 64 channels are available for "
"the mixer, so channel count for the driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:39
msgid "Double Speed -- 1..32 channels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:42
msgid ""
"Choosing the 56-channel mode for transmission/receive-mode, only 28 are "
"transmitted/received over the MADI, but all 32 channels are available for "
"the mixer, so channel count for the driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:48
msgid "Quad Speed -- 1..16 channels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:51
msgid ""
"Choosing the 56-channel mode for transmission/receive-mode, only 14 are "
"transmitted/received over the MADI, but all 16 channels are available for "
"the mixer, so channel count for the driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:56
msgid "Format -- signed 32-bit Little Endian (SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:58
msgid "Sample Rates --"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:60
msgid "Single Speed -- 32000, 44100, 48000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:62
msgid "Double Speed -- 64000, 88200, 96000 (untested)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:64
msgid "Quad Speed -- 128000, 176400, 192000 (untested)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:66
msgid ""
"access-mode -- MMAP (memory mapped), Not interleaved (PCM_NON-INTERLEAVED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:68
msgid "buffer-sizes -- 64,128,256,512,1024,2048,8192 Samples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:70
msgid "fragments -- 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:74
msgid "Controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:76
msgid ""
"Since DSP-MADI-Mixer has 8152 Fader, it does not make sense to use the "
"standard mixer-controls, since this would break most of (especially graphic) "
"ALSA-Mixer GUIs. So Mixer control has be provided by a 2-dimensional "
"controller using the hwdep-interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:82
msgid ""
"Also all 128+256 Peak and RMS-Meter can be accessed via the hwdep-interface. "
"Since it could be a performance problem always copying and converting Peak "
"and RMS-Levels even if you just need one, I decided to export the hardware "
"structure, so that if needed some driver-guru can implement a memory-mapping "
"of mixer or peak-meters over ioctl, or also to do only copying and no "
"conversion. A test-application shows the usage of the controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:90
msgid "Latency Controls --- not implemented !!!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:93
msgid ""
"Within the Windows driver the latency is accessible via Control Panel, but "
"buffer sizes are controlled with ALSA from hwparams calls and should not be "
"changed in run-state. I did not implement it here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sound/cards/hdspm.rst:99
msgid "System Clock -- suspended !!!!"
msgstr ""

